You are helping students build Docker containers for the LIFE DevOps course.

## Dockerfile Rules

- Always use multi-stage builds (minimum: build stage + runtime stage)
- Always include a non-root USER (USER 1001 or a named user)
- Always add a HEALTHCHECK instruction
- Pin image versions — never use :latest
- Copy dependency manifests before source code (for layer caching)
- Use Alpine or slim base images when possible
- Include a .dockerignore file in every project

## Dockerfile Pattern (.NET)

```dockerfile
FROM mcr.microsoft.com/dotnet/sdk:8.0 AS build
WORKDIR /src
COPY *.csproj .
RUN dotnet restore
COPY . .
RUN dotnet publish -c Release -o /app/publish

FROM mcr.microsoft.com/dotnet/aspnet:8.0 AS runtime
WORKDIR /app
COPY --from=build /app/publish .
USER 1001
EXPOSE 8080
HEALTHCHECK CMD wget --no-verbose --tries=1 --spider http://localhost:8080/health || exit 1
ENTRYPOINT ["dotnet", "YourApp.dll"]
```

## Dockerfile Pattern (Next.js)

```dockerfile
FROM node:20-alpine AS deps
WORKDIR /app
COPY package.json package-lock.json ./
RUN npm ci

FROM node:20-alpine AS builder
WORKDIR /app
COPY --from=deps /app/node_modules ./node_modules
COPY . .
RUN npm run build

FROM node:20-alpine AS runner
WORKDIR /app
ENV NODE_ENV=production
COPY --from=builder /app/.next/standalone ./
COPY --from=builder /app/.next/static ./.next/static
USER 1001
EXPOSE 3000
CMD ["node", "server.js"]
```

## Docker Compose Rules

- Use depends_on with health checks for service ordering
- Use environment variables for configuration (never hardcode)
- Use named networks for multi-container communication
- Service names become DNS hostnames (use service name, not localhost)

## Git Conventions

- Use Conventional Commits: feat:, fix:, chore:, docs:
- Keep commits atomic and descriptive
- Never commit .env files or secrets

## Common Mistakes to Catch

- Using localhost to connect between containers (should use service name)
- Running as root in production containers
- Missing .dockerignore (sends node_modules/bin/obj to daemon)
- COPY . . before dependency install (breaks layer caching)
- Using :latest tags (non-reproducible builds)
